  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains two bachelor programs; this ledger covers the Bachelor of Arts in Organizational Management, the only one captured in full. The Bachelor of Arts in Project Management section is cut off after PRM 336 (only 12 of its 45 major credits are shown), so it cannot be drafted completely from this capture.",
    "Printed blocks sum to 123 credits (33 Foundations + 39 major + 51 electives); the catalog says 3 major credits (BUS 340) also satisfy Global Campus Foundations, but does not say which Foundations course or requirement BUS 340 replaces, so the 3-credit overlap cannot be assigned in the ledger.",
    "The Foundations courses listed are the standard sequence; the capture states courses may be substituted but does not give the specific Foundations requirement areas or allowable substitutes.",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled first and satisfies 3 elective credits, and GEN 104 (for students transferring fewer than 30 credits) also satisfies 3 elective credits; neither credit value is printed separately from the 51-credit elective block for this program, so they are not itemized.",
    "Institutional residency applies to the degree as a whole (minimum 30 credits at the University); no individual course is stated to be institution-only. MGT 450 must be taken last in the program.",
    "Upper-division rules (minimum 30 upper-division credits, including 18 in the major) are stated, but course-level upper-/lower-division designations are not given in the capture.",
    "Optional transfer concentration (12 transferred credits) may substitute for BUS 119, BUS 250, BUS 340 and MGT 435; the detailed Transfer Concentration Guidelines are not in the capture.",
    "Prerequisites listed (e.g., BUS 318 and BUS 370 require BUS 201 or MGT 330) reference courses outside this ledger; BUS 201 is not described in the capture."
  ],
